{#- Expects `interface` in scope. `interface.mlag_id` is the lag_id of a host-facing port-channel of an MLAG pair
    (transforms/helpers/vxlan.py), the same on both peers; it is never set on the peer-link.
    D: Arista EOS User Manual, Multi-chassis Link Aggregation (arista.com/en/um-eos/eos-multi-chassis-link-aggregation),
    "MLAG Interface Configuration Commands": `mlag <id>` under `interface Port-Channel <n>` (the manual's example is
    `mlag 12` under `interface port-channel 20`). "Configuring MLAG Services": "Port channels configured as an MLAG
    must have identical port channel numbers", and the best practice is to set the MLAG ID to the port channel
    number, which is what lag_id is on both peers. The peer-link is bound by `peer-link` (arista_eos_mlag.j2). -#}
{%- if interface.mlag_id is defined %}
   mlag {{ interface.mlag_id }}
{%- endif -%}
